message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on brake pad shims. Brake pad shims are parts of disc brakes, so the likely heading is 8708.30 (parts and accessories of motor vehicles: brakes and servo-brakes; parts thereof). Within that, 8708.30.50 covers "other" brakes and parts, with statistical suffixes: 8708.30.5010 for brake linings (assembled) and 8708.30.5090 for other. The 8708.30.10 subheading covers mounted brake linings, and I'm uncertain whether a shim would fall there. The "other" 8708.30.50 is the better fit.

Recalling the 2019-2020 reorganization: 8708.30.5000 is the "Other" subheading, with 8708.30.5010 for brake system parts, so I'll settle on 8708.30.5090 as the residual statistical line.

{"hts_code": "8708.30.5090", "reason": "Brake pad shims of rubber, steel and adhesive are parts of motor vehicle disc brakes, classified in heading 8708 as other parts of brakes under subheading 8708.30.50."}
